cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  esf-recoverability: reference implementation, probes and per-recording
  results for Dammu, "ESF: Harmonizing Heterogeneous EEG Acquisition for
  Pretrained Classifiers", preprint v2 (September 2026).
message: >-
  If you use this code, the probes, the per-recording predictions or the
  acquisition operators, please cite the preprint (preferred) and this
  software archive.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Hitesh
    family-names: Dammu
    email: hdammu@asu.edu
    affiliation: Independent Researcher, Hyderabad, India
repository-code: 'https://github.com/h5371h/esf-recoverability'
url: 'https://github.com/h5371h/esf-recoverability'
abstract: >-
  A measurement protocol for a fixed EEG preprocessing contract (the
  Encephlian Standard Format, ESF). Five acquisition differences (native
  sampling rate, gain, mains interference, electrode montage, broadband
  noise) are simulated on raw microvolt TUAB evaluation recordings and
  three frozen public models (EEGPT, LaBraM, BIOT), each with four
  probes trained on the TUAB train split only, are scored with the full
  contract and with the one corrective step that addresses each
  difference switched off. The repository releases the contract, the
  operators, the model adapters, all twelve probes, every per-recording
  prediction, the permuted-label and outlyingness controls, the
  class-conditional AUROC-TV bound check, the CPU cost benchmark and the
  scripts that regenerate every table and figure of the preprint. v2
  supersedes v1 (tag v1.0.0-spmb2026-submission), which was withdrawn
  from IEEE SPMB 2026 by the author; see the preprint's Version note.
keywords:
  - electroencephalography
  - EEG
  - acquisition shift
  - preprocessing contract
  - pretrained models
  - reproducibility
